{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And it shall be when he cries out to Me.</b> Because he [the poor man] cries out against Me [HaShem] and says: You created me just like him, yet he sleeps on my bed in comfort while I have nothing to sleep on. However, the expression ״שמעתי כי חנון אני״ [for I will hear, for I am gracious] does not fit well with this explanation. Therefore it seems preferable to explain that it refers to what precedes: ״עד בא השמש״ etc. — and if you do so [return the pledge], ״והיה כי יצעק אלי״ — and he cries out to Me and prays concerning you, for all the good you did for him, ״ושמעתי תפלתו כי חנון אני״ — and I will hear his prayer, for I am gracious: just as you showed compassion to this one, I, who am called gracious, will have compassion and show grace to you and bless you. As it is said: ״ואברכך״. And so too it is written: ״כי בגלל הדבר הזה יברכך ה' אלהיך״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase והה\"ד (והא הדא) appears to introduce a prooftext for the blessing; the parenthetical ואברכך may be the cited text itself."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:58.669019601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}